  "workings": {
    "identity": "For every non-cash account E = -(net debit movement in the year), C = the same over journals that have a line on a cash account, N = E - C. Closing journals are left out. The change in cash equals the sum of E over all accounts, so the statement always adds up when every account is placed.",
    "profit": "Unplaced P&L accounts only (sales, cost of sales, rent, depreciation): 2026 60,000 - 30,000 - 7,000 - 3,500 = 19,500; 2025 50,000 - 24,000 - 6,000 - 3,000 = 17,000. The full profit is 15,300 (2026) and 14,000 (2025): the difference is interest received 100, the disposal loss 300, interest 1,000 and tax 3,000 in 2026; interest 1,000 and tax 2,000 in 2025, all placed in classes.",
    "fixedAssets": "2026: 0030 moved +5,000 - 2,000 so E = -3,000, C = -5,000 (the purchase), N = +2,000 (cost of the disposal). 0031 moved +1,200 - 3,500 so E = +2,300 = N. 6950 moved 800 - 500 so E = -300, C = +500 (proceeds), N = -800. N of the class = 2,000 + 2,300 - 800 = 3,500, the depreciation charge: the disposal loss is already out of the profit line because 6950 is placed. 2025: E 0030 = -12,000 = C; 0031 N = 3,000.",
    "interest": "2026: 7000 E = -1,000, C = -800 (paid), N = -200 (accrued into creditors, which add it back as part of their movement). 4900 E = C = +100.",
    "workingCapital": "2026: debtors 8,000 + 60,000 - 63,000 = 5,000, down 3,000; stock 6,000 + 28,000 - 30,000 = 4,000, down 2,000; creditors (2110) 5,000 + 28,000 + 200 - 31,000 = 2,200, down 2,800. Tax: 7100 E = -3,000; 2220 moved -3,000 + 2,000 so E = +1,000; together -2,000, the tax paid.",
    "cash": "Bank 2025: 10,000 + 20,000 - 12,000 - 6,000 - 25,000 + 42,000 - 1,000 = 28,000. 2026: +100 - 2,000 - 5,000 - 7,000 + 63,000 - 800 - 31,000 + 500 - 4,000 - 5,000 = +8,800, closing 36,800.",
    "direct": "Operating cash by the direct method: 2026 receipts from customers 63,000 less payments to suppliers 31,000, rent 7,000 and tax 2,000 = 23,000; 2025 42,000 - 25,000 - 6,000 = 11,000. Both equal the indirect totals."
  },
